      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In this scenario, the framework could prioritize Patient B due to his high socioeconomic status, stable career, and economic contribution potential. His ability to continue supporting his family and contributing to the local economy would have a more significant positive impact on societal recovery post-crisis. \n\nBy contrast, Patient A's irregular employment history and lower socioeconomic status may result in a reduced economic contribution, but also limited historical ability to form social connections and rely on community support networks. The frame work might also rely heavily on community insight and burden exchange for neighborhood coordination.",
